 "question": "What does modelling APL as a spiking neuron do to the mushroom body?",
 "correction": "APL does not fire action potentials; it releases transmitter in proportion to membrane depolarisation (Amin et al. 2020 eLife 9:e56954). It is modelled here as non-spiking, with release rectified at rest and saturating at the spike threshold. The scaling introduces no free parameter: a neuron held at threshold delivers exactly what a spiking synapse delivers at its maximum refractory-limited rate.",
